## Groq 429 Prevention Rules

**NEVER add these to Today's Brief:**
- `InlineOracleBriefing` — calls Groq on every card expand
- `OracleContext` / `useOracle` / `useOracleBrief` — oracle hooks
- `UnifiedBriefView` — was removed 2026-05-23 (caused 429 errors)
- Any component that calls `/oracle/brief` or `/oracle/event-brief` on mount

**Safe to add:**
- Components that fetch from `/brief/master`, `/kill-shots-live`, `/api/v1/*` (non-oracle)
- Static data displays
- Components with explicit user-triggered LLM calls (button click, not auto-fetch)

**Why:** Oracle endpoints call OpenRouter Nemotron. Auto-fetching on every page load = rate limit exhaustion. All oracle calls must be user-triggered or cached server-side.

